Stage 1: Basic Network & Messaging (Single Device, Multi-Session)
1. Objective

Build a minimal chat network where two users can connect, log in with different identities, and exchange messages in real-time. Testing will be done on a single device using two browser sessions (e.g., Chrome normal + Chrome Incognito).

2. Scope

Develop a Node.js server with Socket.IO for WebSocket communication.

Create a simple frontend (HTML + JS) for user login and messaging.

Enable two distinct users to log in and exchange messages in real-time.

Store only in-memory session data (no database at this stage).

3. Features
3.1 User Login

User enters a username (e.g., “Alice”, “Bob”).

Server assigns session ID.

Multiple users can connect simultaneously.

3.2 Real-time Messaging

Users can send text messages.

Messages are broadcast only to the recipient (not all users).

Show sender + message in chat window.

3.3 Basic UI

One-page HTML app:

Username input & “Join” button.

Chat window (messages).

Input box + send button.

4. Non-Goals (Stage 1)

No file sharing (images, PDFs, etc.).

No message encryption.

No database or persistence.

No security features beyond session IDs.

No steganography detection (that’s a later stage).

5. User Flow

Start server: node server.js.

Open Chrome normal tab, log in as “Alice.”

Open Chrome Incognito, log in as “Bob.”

Alice sends message → Bob sees it instantly.

Bob replies → Alice sees it instantly.

6. Technical Requirements
6.1 Backend

Node.js with Express + Socket.IO.

Handles user connections and message events.

Maintains in-memory list of active users.

6.2 Frontend

HTML + CSS + Vanilla JS.

Connects to WebSocket server via Socket.IO client.

Renders chat messages in real-time.

6.3 Example Message Flow
{
  "from": "Alice",
  "to": "Bob",
  "message": "Hello Bob!"
}

7. Testing Strategy

Run server locally on localhost:3000.

Open two sessions:

Normal browser → login as Alice.

Incognito browser → login as Bob.

Send messages between sessions.

Validate:

Messages are delivered instantly.

Each user sees only relevant chat messages.

8. Success Criteria

✅ Two users can log in on the same device.
✅ Messages are sent and received in real-time.
✅ Each user sees their chat history during session.